    "done_when": "Run `date -u` first and treat that instant as your start; your deadline is 60 minutes later. Write your manifest before starting any long command. Rescan into docs/research/data/local-lane-deaths.json with docs/research/scripts/scan_local_lane_deaths.py, in the foreground under `timeout 1200`, using the after window the script now supports (since 2026-09-30T18:36:00Z), so the committed data file's after block carries the figures the research page states (343 reviews and 17 deaths at the time of the first scan; a rescan may count more) and its after_state no longer reads not_produced. Every figure on docs/research/local-lane-death-rate.html that reads the data file then agrees with it; update the page's figures if the rescan's counts moved. The page states the rerun of the before window as 393 of 1343 against the published 392 of 1333, with the reason (runs dispatched before the move and resumed after it), rather than saying it reproduces the published rate. tests/test_death_scan_after_window.py builds a temporary runs root with synthesised review run directories on both sides of a cutoff and asserts the after window's count, death count, Wilson interval and the not-yet-measurable state below 60 reviews; it fails if the windowing is removed. Run that test and tests/test_the_local_lane_death_rate_is_stated.py at base and head, each in the foreground with its own basetemp, logs ending with a bare EXIT= line. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
